Reason: a GameMaker 1 room keeps every tile in the draw list (rm_a5h04: ~2,300), and 1.5.5's wide mode draws the room
twice, the first time into a surface it never shows. The Wii port already drops those draws, but the runner still
walked each tile to reach it: the layer lookup, the tile record and a renderer call, ~2,300 times a frame for nothing.
A renderer can now say its current target is thrown away; the runner then passes over the whole run of tiles at once
(no GML runs between neighboring tiles, so the answer holds for the run). Nothing else changes.
Upstream: New optional renderer hook, every platform; nothing changes for renderers that leave it unset. Retires this patch when merged.

